WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.770
Jill sensed that the Fantasia 
was vanishing from the forest,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.030
so she gathered up all of
the Fantasia she had left...

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.580
to keep them safe.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.660
They're still little, 
so we've gotta keep them safe.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:20.950
What is it?

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.610
I must thank you.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.930
Wh-What's this all about? 
You're embarrassing me.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:31.260
I was about to kill my own children.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:38.930
But the Fantasia in here 
will soon disappear, as well.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:42.220
Can't you just make a new cocoon for them?

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:47.690
Even making a single cocoon 
takes many centuries.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.180
But time doesn't mean anything 
in this forest, right?

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.020
This forest is now adjacent to human land.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.700
With Jill, it might have been possible,

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.710
but I can't do it alone.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.130
Why not?

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.210
Don't act all defeated. 
This isn't like you.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.960
I'm... half human.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:46.020
<b>The Future Is With You 
-Eternity-</b>

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.670
<i>"The Future Is With You."</i>

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:50.270
Half... human?

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.520
My father was a real trickster.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.280
He transformed himself 
and courted human women.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.780
To his surprise, 
one of them got pregnant.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:08.230
I'll let you imagine 
the details for yourself,

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.570
but that's the reason I'm here.

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:14.290
When the other young ones 
dissolved away,

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:18.210
I couldn't follow them...

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:21.050
because I am half human.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:25.870
For an extraordinarily long time, 
I was all alone.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:30.310
I tried to join my brethren, 
but nothing worked.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:35.890
Whenever humans appeared, 
they attacked without a second thought,

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.070
and they never stopped coming.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.730
That was when I met Jill.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.830
She advised me against what I was doing, 
and thanks to her,

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:49.290
I eventually lost interest 
in attacking the humans.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:56.090
Instead, I decided I wanted 
to create some new little ones.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:02.220
To please Jill, I even started 
paying visits to the castle.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:06.650
Then the humans started spreading their own

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:09.980
thoughtless explanations about my presence.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.980
Then the legend of the great Merlin...

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:20.130
There was a time, long ago, when I 
encountered some very combative humans.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.990
I chased them away,

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:29.990
but the humans I saved had the mistaken idea 
that I did it to protect them.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.660
Long after that, 
some of them approached me

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:36.910
and said they wanted the forest 
in exchange for money.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:40.660
But this land never belonged 
to anyone in the first place!

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:45.130
Just look at how that story 
has been handed down...

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:47.940
An old man, riding a stag,

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:53.470
saying noble things like 
"I will not divide this land,"

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:55.890
as if he were protecting it!

00:04:55.890 --> 00:05:00.480
Huh? You mean all the stories 
they passed down were misunderstandings?

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.170
That's exactly it.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:07.990
First of all, my name isn't Merlin. 
It's Myrddin!

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:10.930
<i>Even his name was remembered wrong?!</i>

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:14.500
<i>Now we can't swear anything 
on Merlin's name!</i>

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:19.330
I'm pretty good 
at making rocks and trees grow,

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:24.260
but I can't create something with life 
that could take in my children.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:30.440
Jill once held me 
as if I were one of her children.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.250
Hey, Myr, do you think 
the opposite could work?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.390
The opposite? 
You mean, have a human carry them?

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:40.490
Yeah. Does that sound weird?

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:42.370
It's not weird!

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:47.650
If Myr is half human, 
then his children are one-fourth human!

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.310
You can't be—

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.910
Actually, you might be right.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:58.420
But that human would have to take in 
massive amounts of Fantasia.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:03.420
You mean if that human were
 a really powerful sorcerer, it would work?

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:07.170
She would have to take this cocoon 
into her body.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:12.180
It won't be so easy to find a sorcerer 
with a belly that big.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.430
Don't worry! I know of one!

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:17.940
Yes...

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:23.440
And that sorcerer would consider it an honor.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:34.830
You have talent!

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.080
In another age, 
we may have been best friends!

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:40.220
You are naïve! 
That would be impossible!

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:43.170
I'm putting this battle on hold. 
Well fought.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:44.420
Wait, you!

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.400
I will not wait!

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.870
In fact, I <i>can't</i> wait!

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.420
I'm about to... 
I'm about to wet myself!

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:53.410
Why did he even come here?

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:55.180
Lord de Gulis, you're safe!

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:58.040
You have been placed under suspicion.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.770
Could we ask you to accompany us?

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:03.720
Great Merlin, 
what is to become of this nation?

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:06.190
Does it have a future?

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:11.800
Both sides are retreating. 
Things seem to have calmed down.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:15.450
Did you know this was going to happen, 
Captain Dragunov?

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:19.660
No. When everyone was facing off 
against that monster...

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:22.460
I thought we were all done for.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:28.960
But if we'd turned our backs, 
our deaths would have been far more tragic.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.990
Captain...

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.800
Time to change course.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:36.470
We should take this opportunity 
to get our own ship out of here.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.890
Y-Yes, sir. Where are we headed?

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.540
To Bome, of course.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:43.080
Can we really go back there?

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.590
We have violated orders so many times.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:48.730
Surely there will be no justifying that.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.490
I'll take care of that.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:56.400
So, on that note, 
our squad is going to be busy for a while.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.990
Please don't be too hard on us.

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.850
If anyone wants out, now's the time.

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.010
Certainly not!

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:06.630
I-I'll always be one of your men, 
Captain Dragunov!

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:11.250
<i>No matter how much authority we have,</i>

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:14.740
<i>trying to enslaving the infected 
is a matter I can't overlook.</i>

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:18.760
<i>I need to find out what 
General Torque's true intentions are.</i>

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:29.020
<b>[The Castle Underground] 
What Seth saw as he was going to meet Diabal... 
looked like the remains of a fierce battle. Where is Diabal...?</b>

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:38.080
A Thaumaturge, eh?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.410
We'll have to handle you with care.

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:43.850
<i>This is humiliating.</i>

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:47.930
<i>But General Torque's thinking is profound.</i>

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:50.380
<i>He won't be fazed by something like this.</i>

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:57.820
<b>3 Days Later</b>

00:08:56.050 --> 00:09:01.630
Three days have passed 
since the Inquisitors meddled in our ceremony

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:05.630
and brought disaster upon this land.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:11.180
Many of our people, 
and much of this land itself, have been lost.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:15.750
However, Caislean Merlin will recover.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:18.170
Let us mourn our dead.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.580
Let us bandage our wounds.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:26.350
And let us celebrate this day 
for all eternity.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:30.750
The day that Cyfandir dealt a painful blow

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:35.340
to those arrogant Inquisitors!

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:40.130
Long live the queen!

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:46.710
That said, we were not
 prepared to go into battle.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:50.610
If not for those from outside
 the kingdom who came to our aid,

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.860
and for the intervention of Merlin himself,

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:58.610
Cyfandir would be on its knees right now.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:03.120
The enemy's scheme planted seeds of doubt 
in our people's hearts

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:07.120
and gave our enemy control 
over our citizens and knights.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.540
It was both cunning and ingenious.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:14.970
If I had not turned my back 
on our customs to this extent...

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:20.140
If I had listened to all of you 
and engaged in the sharing of opinions...

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.640
Perhaps such a conspiracy 
would not have come about.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:28.640
Above all, if we had not 
kept our curses hidden,

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:34.150
perhaps those who plotted to sacrifice
 our kingdom for profit would not have come.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:40.160
People of Cyfandir, 
now is the time to take off our masks!

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.230
What's going on?

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:50.900
It's that apprentice, Ocoho!

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:57.110
I have...

00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:00.430
a mark just below my ear.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:05.930
When someone touches it, 
I have no choice but to do their bidding,

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.690
and I have no memory of 
what happens while in that state.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:19.110
I have six breasts.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:22.450
Two are where they should be...

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:25.420
H-Hey, should you really be sharing this?

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.690
Brangoire! Where are the other four?!

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.610
We're curious now!

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.830
I-I can't tell you that!

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.120
Under your beard?

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:35.090
I won't say!

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.840
My hair is actually blue.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:42.090
Um, my queen, I think you made that up.

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.350
Tell us what your curse is!

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.310
You'll find out soon enough.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.610
We want to hear it straight from you!

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.910
Goodness... 
Well, you see, my curse is...

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:58.600
that I grow more beautiful by the day!

00:11:58.600 --> 00:12:00.210
Yeah, I believe that!

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:01.740
Liar!

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:05.070
Are you saying the queen 
doesn't grow more beautiful by the day?!

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:07.140
That's not her curse, though!

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:08.620
Maybe not, but still!

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:12.250
My hair... is harder than steel!

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.810
I have claws instead of teeth!

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:19.830
I have two necks, but only one head!

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.260
I have two nostrils, but only one nose!

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:24.130
That's normal!

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:26.220
All right, all right!

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.390
Let's save the confessions for later!

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:32.040
U-Um... Your Majesty, can I ask you something?

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:34.390
Are you, by any chance... expecting?

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:38.650
Oh, my. 
I can't hide anything from all of you.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.650
But isn't it too sudden?

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:42.150
Who's the father?

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:45.190
The father wishes to remain anonymous.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:48.180
He's a short, bearded man

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:51.340
and a proud guardian of Cyfandir.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:54.580
He lives in all of your hearts.

00:12:56.570 --> 00:12:59.420
Does he have boobs under his beard?

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:03.300
Fool! Are you suggesting 
I would make a move on the queen?!

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:05.430
You wouldn't?

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:08.140
I mean, of course, if I had the chance...

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.510
Wait, huh?!

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:12.560
Wh-What I meant was, um, that is...

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.720
Brangoire's turning redder and redder!

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:16.790
Quiet!

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:20.550
First of all, stop speaking to the queen 
with such a lack of respect!

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:21.710
And second...

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:23.820
Well, you know...

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.070
Huh? We can't hear you!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.700
Second...

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:30.580
Your Majesty, I have a favor to ask.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.120
What is it?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:36.030
I wish to retract the deferment that 
I declared during the ordination ceremony.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:40.780
The one regarding the recommendation 
of the apprentice Ocoho.

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:41.710
Huh?

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:47.740
Unfortunately, all the knights 
have already chosen their heirs.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.470
But I have not.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:53.970
Huh? Y-You're making me... your heir?

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:57.910
My, that is quite a surprise, Brangoire.

00:13:57.910 --> 00:13:59.230
But you cannot.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:05.360
She was the one who brought the conspiracy 
involving the Spectres to light!

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:09.740
She faced the Merchant Barons 
all by herself!

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:14.120
She ran them out of the country 
with no concern for her own curse!

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:19.880
Ocoho's Gysoni is more powerful 
than any I've ever seen!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:25.510
But Ocoho defied your orders in battle, 
did she not?

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:27.970
She did it to protect the farmers!

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.390
She slapped her queen in the face.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:33.010
She did that to return you to your senses!

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:37.780
At the ordination ceremony, 
she tried to make you commit mutiny against me.

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:39.770
She did it to protect the people!

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:43.150
My mind is already made up.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:47.150
She has the kind of talent 
that surfaces only once every several centuries!

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:49.190
Brangoire!

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:53.990
Shame on you for trying to make
 Ocoho one of Merlin's knights!

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.910
It is a disgrace to the people of Cyfandir!

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:02.730
Her Majesty is right.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:06.800
I've done too much to be forgiven.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.270
Lord Brangoire...

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:12.310
I'm sorry I can't repay your kindness.

00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:14.430
What nonsense is this?

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:19.180
I have been observing your behavior 
for a long time.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:23.860
You were never fit to become a knight.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:26.670
You are...

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:30.950
someone worthy of being the queen.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:35.370
What?!

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:42.540
Not only for the accomplishments 
Brangoire just named.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.420
At the ordination ceremony,

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:48.880
you defied me 
for the good of the people.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:52.630
But... you seemed really angry.

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:54.970
That was just a joke.

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:57.390
I liked you so much, 
I wanted to eat you up!

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:01.940
If I didn't make someone 
as capable as you my heir,

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:04.930
I would completely lose face.

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:08.400
Even mirrors would refuse
to show my reflection anymore.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.900
Eh? H-Huh?!

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:15.430
People of Cyfandir, your future queen...

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:17.530
and my heir!

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:19.210
Princess Ocoho!

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:29.800
<b>Ocoho 
Princess and Successor to the Throne of Cyfandir</b>

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:31.550
Cheers to Ocoho!

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:34.050
Long live the princess!

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:36.410
She's embarrassed! How cute!

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.730
Hooray for the cute Princess Ocoho!

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:40.640
Long live the pretty girl!

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.770
Hey! Don't be rude to my princess!

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:46.820
Long live the six-boobed Brangoire!

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:48.820
Enough about the boobs!

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:51.330
I have no idea what's going on anymore.

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:53.450
I don't know what has happened,

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:57.890
but you have bloomed beautifully 
in these past few weeks.

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:00.880
You stopped worrying 
about your superiors' opinions,

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:03.330
abandoned the acknowledgment 
you had wished for,

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:06.580
and overcame yourself.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:11.090
That was all thanks to—

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:12.340
I said back off!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:12.340
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.840
Wait, where's Seth?

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:33.110
The future queen?

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:36.060
That's a fantastic decision.

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:38.420
Ocoho probably doesn't remember it,

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:41.370
but she came to the forest often as a child.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.950
If all humans were like her,

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:49.880
I'm sure they would have made an effort 
to protect the forest.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:52.630
But it's too late now.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.200
It might not be.

00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:57.490
When your children are eventually born,

00:17:57.490 --> 00:18:02.390
maybe they'll be able to use their powers 
to rebuild Caillte's forest.

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:05.890
Jill is gone, though.

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:08.170
If I hadn't come here,

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:12.020
the Inquisitors probably 
wouldn't have come here, either.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:13.810
Sorry.

00:18:13.810 --> 00:18:15.900
Don't blame yourself.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.830
It would've happened eventually.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:20.990
Besides, if you hadn't stopped me,

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:23.660
I would have destroyed everything.

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:29.290
And then I would have lost my children, too.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:32.950
Don't make that face!

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:37.450
All right! I'll play you a song 
I wrote with Jill in mind!

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:40.550
I call it "A Thousand Times, At Least"!

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:43.810
Hang on, Myr! 
I never said I wanted to hear—

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:47.350
Oh, Jill!

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:50.490
When I lean upon your chest,

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:55.820
the centuries pass by like mere hours!

00:18:56.530 --> 00:19:04.940
If this time that passes by 
is an eternity to the humans,

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:11.510
I wish my relationship with you 
could have lasted an eternity, too.

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:16.450
A thousand times, at least...

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:29.210
Seth, here's the Magosia stone 
you were looking for.

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:31.350
Is this really all you want?

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:33.380
Yeah! Thanks!

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:35.460
Grimm will be really happy.

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:36.860
This is for Melie.

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:42.360
The best craftsmen in the kingdom 
worked hard to make it.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:45.110
Thank you, Your Majesty.

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:46.120
Please, stop.

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:49.120
You're making the mood too somber.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.620
Such formality isn't needed between us.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.880
And me? Got anything for me?

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.120
Of course, Doc.

00:19:57.120 --> 00:20:01.280
This is to thank you 
for saving this nation from crisis.

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:04.350
It grants you the honorary title 
of a knight of this kingdom.

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:08.640
Now, no matter where you go, 
you are a Knight-sorcerer.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:12.140
Um... Maybe something else...

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:14.650
But that's great, Doc! You're a knight!

00:20:14.650 --> 00:20:17.500
Yeah, but... I mean...

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:20.980
Maybe some gold 
to help me pay off my debt...

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:22.150
No?

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.060
I can't do that.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:28.150
We have to rebuild this city.

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:32.160
It seems Brangoire has
 a little gift for you, too.

00:20:35.220 --> 00:20:37.170
What is it? A pebble?

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:39.670
It's the armor of Pen Draig.

00:20:42.230 --> 00:20:44.290
<i>If there comes a time 
when you must fight...</i>

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:46.500
<i>...you'll need to fight with armor on!</i>

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:48.430
I hear weird voices coming from Doc!

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.890
Is it the stones I swallowed?!

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:54.420
You are the only one 
capable of using it.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:55.610
Take it.

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:59.400
I'll need you to protect 
the princess from now on.

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:01.830
We've prepared your steed.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:05.660
Huh? What's going on?

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:09.260
My thoughts have always been with my people,

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:14.030
but I was unable to realize 
that a conspiracy was brewing.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:18.670
My perspective was not broad enough 
to see all that was happening.

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:21.670
Ocoho, go with them.

00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:25.360
Go and see the entirety of this vast world,

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:27.670
so that you don't make the same mistake I did.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:33.330
Okay, we're off!

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:35.180
Thank you for everything!

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:37.440
Be well, Your Majesty!

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.750
Of course. Same to you, Your Majesty.

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:43.690
May Cyfandir have...

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:45.320
...a bright future!

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:47.830
Hey!

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:51.380
If anyone lays so much 
as one finger on the princess,

00:21:51.380 --> 00:21:53.930
they'll get the death penalty!

00:21:53.930 --> 00:21:55.960
That goes for all of you, too!

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:59.780
And you'd better take good care 
of the queen's belly!

00:21:59.780 --> 00:22:02.680
Those little ones are basically my siblings!

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:04.210
Be careful with them!

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:07.670
Why can't they both just say 
they'll be counting on each other?

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:11.720
<i>They may be like your siblings,</i>

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:15.730
<i>but don't forget that 
they're my children.</i>

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:18.270
<i>Go on, and don't worry about a thing.</i>

00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:20.480
<i>I'll be watching over them.</i>

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:40.180
This is the first time 
I've ever left Cyfandir!

00:22:44.030 --> 00:22:45.930
She's just like you when 
we first met, Seth.

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:46.840
Huh?

00:22:46.840 --> 00:22:49.090
Is that what I was like?

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:52.720
Yes, but you've changed quite a bit.

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:54.230
So have you.

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:56.830
Everyone grows up,

00:22:56.830 --> 00:22:59.100
by overcoming all kinds of things.

00:22:59.810 --> 00:23:02.060
I'm glad you came to help me out.

00:23:02.060 --> 00:23:05.240
If I'd been on my own, 
I would've lost all control.

00:23:05.240 --> 00:23:08.610
I didn't come just to help you.

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:10.170
I know that.

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:12.120
Thanks, though.

00:23:12.430 --> 00:23:13.850
Thank you, too.

00:23:13.850 --> 00:23:16.120
I'll continue to count on you 
from now on, Seth!

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:18.090
Greetings.

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:21.420
Jeez, don't show up out of nowhere like that!

00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:23.520
Oh, right. Here.

00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:27.430
Ah, Magosia's stone. Thank you.

00:23:27.430 --> 00:23:30.130
That stone was really hard to get, you know?

00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:33.510
So tell me something 
about yourself sometime.

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:35.640
Grimm shall think about it.

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:39.990
Still, even the castle archive 
didn't have any info about Radiant.

00:23:39.990 --> 00:23:42.090
It was all a waste of time.

00:23:42.090 --> 00:23:43.730
What are you talking about?

00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:46.750
You got a wonderful new friend! 
Namely, me!

00:23:46.750 --> 00:23:47.400
Right!

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:51.220
Okay, everyone, 
let's get this adventure started!

00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:53.410
You're so excited.

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:54.700
Of course!

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:58.210
I'll even find Radiant for you!

00:23:58.210 --> 00:24:00.750
Let's see lots of different places!

00:24:02.060 --> 00:24:04.250
Your wish is our command, Princess!

00:24:04.560 --> 00:24:05.750
All right!

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:10.730
Um, can I just go home?

00:24:10.730 --> 00:24:11.920
<i>Nope!</i>

00:24:11.920 --> 00:24:13.260
Why?

00:24:14.970 --> 00:24:17.010
Okay, everyone, let's go!

00:24:17.370 --> 00:24:20.030
Just wait for us, Radiant!

00:24:20.030 --> 00:24:25.020
The Adventure Continues

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>See you again someday!!</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>End</b>
